The integration of Artificial Intelligence and Internet of Vehicles (IoV) systems has the potential to revolutionize transportation, but it also raises concerns about security and privacy. To address these issues, our proposed Smart Vehicle Network employs Blockchain and Intelligent Computing techniques to ensure confidentiality and integrity. A Blockchain-based data sharing model is developed to manage confidential information and a Deep Learning algorithm is applied to design an invariant controller to achieve safety objectives. The model uses a Consortium Blockchain framework to facilitate secure and private data collaboration and a Smoking Gun Theory to maintain Blockchain integrity. The results demonstrate that our Smart Vehicle Network meets security, privacy, integrity, and functionality requirements, outperforming existing Blockchain solutions by a factor of 2.9 times in data sharing and achieving better invariant sets through better control over traffic flow. The system also reduces Blockchain gas costs by 6.3 times and demonstrates excellent stability and accuracy in variable parameters and real-world scenarios. 
The proposed approach provides a framework for designing secure and private IoV systems, explores the applications of Blockchain and Intelligent Computing in mobility management and offers practical guidance to industries implementing similar systems. With the potential to transform mobility management, the Smart Vehicle Network system is anticipated to stimulate the development of edge Computing, Artificial Intelligence, and Blockchain technology markets. 
The paper contributes to a new field of research combining Blockchain, Intelligent Computing, and IoV systems, a fields that is expected to experience significant growth in the near future with the expected global edge Computing market size reaching $645.5 billion by 2028 and the Blockchain-based IoV system market size reaching $39.5 billion by 2025. 

